    "done_when": "Four things hold at the node head.\n\n(1) Every conversion or key access on a row field in reckon/crew/pace_replay.py routes through one guarded reader. A grep of the module for bare float(, int( and fromisoformat( on row values finds none outside that reader.\n\n(2) tests/test_pace_replay.py has a table-driven test. It builds one pace row through the producer's own write path. It takes the field list from that row's keys, so a new field is covered with no edit to the test. For each field and each garbage value (None, \"x\", [], {}, -1) it asserts three things: the week replay returns, that row reads unmeasured with a non-empty reason, and the untouched rows still replay and match.\n\n(3) That test fails at d4eee48b9869d5991f8736e9c4033a360cc33a2f, logged, and passes at the head.\n\n(4) The gate runs `/home/ITER/mcintos/Code/reckon/.venv/bin/python -m pytest -p no:cacheprovider -q tests/test_pace_replay.py tests/test_dispatch_records_the_pace_row.py` from the worktree and exits 0. Its log sits under the run's reports directory.\n\nThe worker appends one anchor to docs/evidence/archive/a-window-paces-the-lane-landed.html by splicing, never by rewriting the file.",
    "estimated_hours": 1.5,
    "goal": "Close the crash class in reckon/crew/pace_replay.py that followup f-awpl-replay-guards-every-row-read names. Every float, int, timestamp parse and key access on a pace-row field must go through one guarded reader. On bad input that reader yields an unmeasured row with a reason, never an exception that takes the whole week's report down. The review at d4eee48b found the surviving site at the float() near line 290. Three earlier rounds each fixed one site of this class, so fix the class rather than the site.",
